  <!-- ============ B2 · WHAT IS INSIDE: ONE PORTAL, THREE MODULES ============ -->
  <section class="band alt" id="inside">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead rv">
        <span class="eyb">What is inside</span>
        <h2>One customer portal. Three modules. Buy one, or run all three.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Performance Management, Service Ticketing and Spare-parts E-commerce are three core modules delivered through the same iSERV customer portal your bakery customers log into. Start with the one your service team needs most, then switch on the others with no new integration, no second login and no second copy of your machine data.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="suite">
        <div class="portal rv">
          <span class="pb-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4M3 9h18"/></svg></span>
          <div class="pb-t">
            <b>iSERV customer portal, under your brand</b>
            <span>One login for every bakery you supply &middot; one record for every oven, mixer and conveyor you have shipped</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pb-tags"><span>Single sign-on</span><span>Shared machine register</span><span>Web, tablet &amp; phone</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="wires" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

        <div class="mods stg">
        <article class="mod">
          <figure class="mod-fig"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Equipment streaming live readings into a dashboard of trend charts, a gauge and an alert bell." width="760" height="487" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
          <div class="mod-h">
            <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4.5 16a8 8 0 1 1 15 0"/><path d="m12 13 3.5-4"/><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="1.4"/><path d="M4 19h16"/></svg></span>
            <span class="no">MODULE 01</span>
            <span class="chip">Available standalone</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Performance Management</h3>
          <p class="mod-l">Live condition of every bakery line you have installed, read straight off the machine.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-chk"/></svg>Real-time line telemetry</b><span>Availability, throughput, OEE and oven thermal health on ovens, mixers and conveyors, benchmarked across your fleet.</span></li>
            <li><b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-chk"/></svg>Predictive maintenance alerts</b><span>Thermal drift, vibration and motor strain flagged while there is still a planned window, before a batch is lost.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="mod">
          <figure class="mod-fig"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="A board of service tickets moving between columns, with an assigned technician, a clock and a calendar." width="760" height="666" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
          <div class="mod-h">
            <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 7.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5.5 6h13A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 20 7.5V10a2 2 0 0 0 0 4v2.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5h-13A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4 16.5V14a2 2 0 0 0 0-4Z"/><path d="M9 10h6M9 14h4"/></svg></span>
            <span class="no">MODULE 02</span>
            <span class="chip">Available standalone</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Service Ticketing</h3>
          <p class="mod-l">Every breakdown and service call in one queue, tied to the machine it came from.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-chk"/></svg>Tickets raised from the machine</b><span>A fault on a tunnel oven or spiral mixer opens a ticket with the machine ID, fault code and recent readings already attached.</span></li>
            <li><b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-chk"/></svg>Tracked through to closed</b><span>Your service desk and field technicians work the same record your customer follows in the portal, with SLA and full machine history.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="mod">
          <figure class="mod-fig"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="A machine exploded into its parts in a 3D viewer, with the selected component going to a cart and out for delivery." width="760" height="672" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
          <div class="mod-h">
            <span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3.5 4.5h2.2l2 10.5h10.3l1.9-7.5H7"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="19" r="1.3"/><circle cx="17" cy="19" r="1.3"/></svg></span>
            <span class="no">MODULE 03</span>
            <span class="chip">Available standalone</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Spare-parts E-commerce</h3>
          <p class="mod-l">Your own parts shop inside the portal, so repeat orders stay with you.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-chk"/></svg>Photo-to-part identification</b><span>Your customer photographs the worn heating element, belt or seal; image recognition and interactive catalogues name the exact part.</span></li>
            <li><b><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-chk"/></svg>One-tap reorder, routed to you</b><span>Pricing, stock and the order land in your system, not a competitor&rsquo;s, so a repeat order takes one tap instead of an email thread.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        </div>

        <div class="combine rv">
          <div>
            <h3>Stronger together, on the same machine record</h3>
            <p>Each module stands on its own. Combined, they hand off to each other automatically: the alert opens the ticket, and the ticket puts the part in the basket.</p>
            <div class="flow" aria-label="Combined workflow example">
              <span><small>Performance</small>Oven 3 heating-zone drift</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-arr"/></svg>
              <span><small>Ticketing</small>Ticket opened, fault attached</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pk-arr"/></svg>
              <span><small>E-commerce</small>HE-4418 element in the basket</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="buy">
            <li><span class="pips" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i></span><b>Start with one module</b><span>Buy only Performance Management, Ticketing or E-commerce and go live on a single line.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pips" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i></i></span><b>Add a second when you are ready</b><span>It switches on inside the same portal, with the same customers, machines and logins already in place.</span></li>
            <li><span class="pips" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i></span><b>Run all three as one platform</b><span>Uptime, service and aftermarket parts revenue managed from a single view of your installed base.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ B3 · CAPABILITIES ============ -->
  <section class="band" id="capabilities">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead rv">
        <span class="eyb">Capabilities</span>
        <h2>What iSERV puts on the bakery line</h2>
        <p class="lede">Telemetry, parts and prediction run off the same connection to the oven, mixer and conveyor. None of it needs a second gateway, a data warehouse, or an engineer on site to read it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid caps rv">

        <div class="caplist">

          <div class="capq open" id="capq-tel">
            <button type="button" class="qh" data-cap="tel" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="capb-tel">
              Real-time bakery line telemetry
              <i aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#pk-chev"/></svg></i>
            </button>
            <div class="qb" id="capb-tel"><div>
              <p>Live availability, throughput and oven thermal health streamed straight from the line, with every machine you have shipped benchmarked against the rest of the fleet.</p>
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip">Exact OEE monitoring</span><span class="chip">Throughput tracking</span><span class="chip">Multi-machine benchmarking</span>
              </div>
            </div></div>
          </div>

