              Predictive maintenance alerts
              <i aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#pk-chev"/></svg></i>
            </button>
            <div class="qb" id="capb-pred"><div>
              <p>Thermal patterns, vibration and motor strain on ovens, mixers and conveyors are read as the line runs, so the alert arrives while there is still a planned window to fix it in - not after the batch has stopped.</p>
              <div class="chips">
                <span class="chip">Thermal pattern analysis</span><span class="chip">Vibration monitoring</span><span class="chip">Wear-and-tear forecasting</span>
              </div>
            </div></div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="cap-med">

            <div class="art on" data-cap="tel">
              <img src="https://dev-website.ithena.app/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/fbb-bakery-line.png" alt="The iSERV dashboard for a bakery line, showing availability, throughput and a loss breakdown for the shift." width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </div>

            <div class="art" data-cap="part">
              <img src="https://dev-website.ithena.app/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/fbb-order.webp" alt="An automated spare-parts ticket raised from live telemetry on a bakery machine, tracked from request through to delivery." width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </div>

            <div class="art" data-cap="pred">
              <img src="https://dev-website.ithena.app/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/fbb-alerts.webp" alt="A commercial bakery line, the equipment iSERV forecasts wear on before a batch is lost." width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
